\begin{center}
{
\Large
Review: More Globs
}
\vspace{0.1in}
\end{center}

\begin{note}
This is a review of the glob from topic01,
plus three new features that are easy to get wrong:
\texttt{glob.iglob} (a generator, not a list),
the \emph{globstar} \texttt{**} (which does nothing special unless you ask for it),
and the \texttt{.gitignore} pattern language (which is \emph{not} the shell glob).
\end{note}

\section{Quick review of the shell glob}

\begin{note}
Recall that the glob is expanded by the shell \emph{before} the program runs,
that \texttt{*} matches any string including the empty string,
that \texttt{?} matches exactly one character,
that \texttt{[abc]} matches one character in the set and \texttt{[\textasciicircum abc]} one character not in the set,
and that \texttt{*} never matches a leading dot.
\end{note}
